    <p>On a single gift the difference is 1,000 UZS, and sending it yourself is cheaper. A ready-made gift saves a few steps and doesn't require buying Stars. For several gifts, the <a href="/en/stars/100">100 Stars pack</a> is handier.</p>
    <div class="post-table-wrap">
      <table class="post-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Quantity</th><th>Ready-made gift (Mini App)</th><th>Stars, sent by you</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>1</td><td>13,000 UZS</td><td>12,000 UZS (50 Stars)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>3</td><td>39,000 UZS</td><td>36,000 UZS (150 Stars)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>5</td><td>65,000 UZS</td><td>60,000 UZS (250 Stars)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>In the Telegram app, 50 Stars cost about $1, but the App Store or Google Play usually asks for an international card. <a href="/en/stars">StarsJoy Stars prices</a> are in Uzbek som.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How long will the Halloween Bear be on sale?</h2>
    <p>There's no exact date, because Telegram hasn't announced one. But seasonal 50-Star bears tend not to stay long:</p>
    <div class="post-table-wrap">
      <table class="post-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Bear (2026)</th><th>Sale period</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Bear with a heart</td><td>Until February 14</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Clown bear</td><td>Until April 1</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bear with a machine gun and bomb</td><td>From August 12, gone by August 17</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>So the Halloween Bear could also disappear within days. That's an estimate, not an official date. While it's on sale, supply is unlimited, so it won't sell out.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Can I get the Halloween Bear after sales end?</h2>
    <p>Once it's removed from Telegram's catalog, you can't buy a new one. Gifts already bought stay with their owners. Regular gifts can't be transferred to someone else either: only collectibles can.</p>
    <p>So be careful if anyone offers this gift "for free" or "at a discount" after sales end. If Telegram opens upgrades later, collectible versions could appear on the market, but that isn't guaranteed.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Can I sell the Halloween Bear or convert it to Stars?</h2>
    <p>You can't sell it on the marketplace, but you can convert it to Stars. The rules:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>What you get back:</strong> about 43 Stars, which is only part of the 50 Stars;</li>
      <li><strong>Time limit:</strong> only for a limited period after receiving it;</li>
      <li><strong>Result:</strong> the gift is permanently destroyed;</li>
      <li><strong>Rating:</strong> under Telegram's rules, your profile rating drops.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No upgrade has been announced as of 2026-10-31.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What changed with the Mask gift?</h2>
    <p>On the same day, Telegram shipped another update: upgrades opened for the 2025 <strong>Mask</strong> gift. That happened on October 31, 2026, at about 20:09 Tashkent time, along with new models for <a href="/en/blog/telegram-gift-crafting">crafting</a>.</p>
    <p>Unlike the Halloween Bear, Mask isn't on primary sale or in the StarsJoy catalog, so you can only get it from existing owners. An unupgraded Mask, which cost 500 Stars in 2025, reached about $36 on third-party platforms (<a href="https://t.me/podarokdurova/8038" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">as of October 31</a>). Prices like this move quickly, so don't treat it as an investment.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What should I watch out for when buying a gift?</h2>
    <p>Never share your Telegram password or SMS code. StarsJoy only needs a username.</p>
    <p>Gift owners face one more risk: fake "I'll buy your gift" messages increased in October. The button in these messages doesn't pay you Stars; it hands your gift to the scammer for free. A <a href="https://t.me/tginfo/4443" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">genuine offer</a> appears in the center of the screen, while a fake one sits on the left like a normal message.</p>
    <p>If an order fails for a technical reason, send your receipt to <a href="https://telegram.me/StarsjoySupport" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@StarsjoySupport</a> within 24 hours for a full refund. More: <a href="/en/blog/is-starsjoy-legit">is StarsJoy legit</a>.</p>
  </section>

